  "title": "Hibernate/Resume Composer Environments, New X-Extra Large Size",
  "summary": "Cloud Composer now allows you to hibernate and resume environments, enabling significant cost savings for development and intermittent workloads. Additionally, a new X-Extra Large environment size is available for more demanding use cases.",
  "details": "Developers can now manage environment costs more effectively with the introduction of `projects.locations.environments.hibernate` and `projects.locations.environments.resume` methods. These new methods allow you to pause and unpause Composer environments, which is particularly useful for development environments or those not running DAGs 24/7. The `name` parameter is required for these new methods, specifying the environment to act upon.\n\nFurthermore, the `EnvironmentConfig` schema now includes a new `ENVIRONMENT_SIZE_X_EXTRA_LARGE` enum value for the `environmentSize` property, providing an additional, larger scaling option for your Composer environments.",
